menu "FreeNet-X Node Configuration"

    config FREENETX_UPLINK_SSID
        string "Uplink Wi-Fi SSID (authorized network)"
        default "MyHomeWiFi"
        help
            SSID of the authorized upstream Wi-Fi network that this node
            connects to. The node shares this uplink with its own AP clients
            via NAPT.

    config FREENETX_UPLINK_PASSWORD
        string "Uplink Wi-Fi password (empty = open network)"
        default "HomePassword456"
        help
            Password for the authorized uplink. Leave empty to join an open
            network that you are permitted to use (for example a public
            hotspot). The node only ever joins the SSID entered above; it
            does not scan for, guess, or capture other networks.

    config FREENETX_AP_SSID
        string "Access point SSID"
        default "FreeNetX-Node-2026"

    config FREENETX_AP_PASSWORD
        string "Access point password (empty = open)"
        default "04012539"
        help
            WPA2 password for the node's own AP. Leave empty for an open AP.

    config FREENETX_NODE_ID
        string "Node ID"
        default "node-001"
        help
            Unique ID for this node, also provisioned in the server's
            FREENETX_NODE_TOKENS environment variable.

    config FREENETX_NODE_TOKEN
        string "Node bearer token"
        default "REPLACE_WITH_UNIQUE_NODE_TOKEN"

    config FREENETX_API_BASE
        string "API base URL"
        default "http://192.168.1.10:8000"
        help
            Base URL of the FreeNet-X server, without a trailing slash.
            Use https:// only if USE_HTTPS is enabled in main.c.

    config FREENETX_SYNC_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Heartbeat interval (ms)"
        range 5000 3600000
        default 30000

    config FREENETX_ADC_SENSOR_GPIO
        int "Analog sensor GPIO (ADC1: 32-39, -1 = disabled)"
        range -1 39
        default 34
        help
            ADC1 pin used to sample an analog sensor. On ESP32 the valid ADC1
            pins are GPIO32..GPIO39 (GPIO34..39 are input-only, which is the
            safest choice). Connect the sensor output here. Set -1 to disable
            sampling. The sample is quantized from float (0..3300 mV) to int8
            and reported in the heartbeat as adc_mv / adc_q.

    config FREENETX_ADC_SENSOR_MIN_MV
        int "Analog sensor range minimum (mV)"
        range 0 3300
        default 0

    config FREENETX_ADC_SENSOR_MAX_MV
        int "Analog sensor range maximum (mV)"
        range 1 3300
        default 3300
        help
            Quantization range used when compressing the ADC sample. Set these
            to the sensor output span you expect (for example 500..2500 mV)
            so the single quantized byte uses its full resolution.

    config FREENETX_INTERNET_CHECK_URL
        string "Internet check URL (empty = disabled)"
        default "http://connectivitycheck.gstatic.com/generate_204"
        help
            The node requests this URL after joining the uplink. Any 2xx/3xx
            response means the uplink really reaches the internet. Leave empty
            to disable the check. Use an endpoint you control if you prefer.

    config FREENETX_CPU_SCALING
        bool "Enable dynamic CPU clock scaling (DFS)"
        default y
        help
            Scales the CPU between the three frequencies the ESP32 supports
            cleanly (80, 160 and 240 MHz) based on measured CPU load. The
            clock is raised automatically around HTTP work and lowered again
            when the node is idle, which reduces heat and USB current.

    config FREENETX_CPU_FREQ_MIN_MHZ
        int "CPU frequency - idle tier (MHz)"
        range 40 240
        default 80
        help
            Frequency used when CPU load is below 30 %%. 80 MHz is the lowest
            frequency the Wi-Fi stack supports cleanly.

    config FREENETX_CPU_FREQ_MED_MHZ
        int "CPU frequency - medium tier (MHz)"
        range 40 240
        default 160
        help
            Frequency used when CPU load is between 30 %% and 70 %%.

    config FREENETX_CPU_FREQ_MAX_MHZ
        int "CPU frequency - high tier (MHz)"
        range 40 240
        default 240
        help
            Frequency used when CPU load is above 70 %%, and during HTTP
            requests. Must be >= the medium tier, which must be >= the idle
            tier. 240/160/80 are the standard ESP32 values.

    config FREENETX_CPU_SCALING_INTERVAL_MS
        int "CPU load sampling interval (ms)"
        range 500 60000
        default 2000
        depends on FREENETX_CPU_SCALING
        help
            How often CPU utilization is measured. Shorter intervals react
            faster but spend slightly more time collecting statistics.

    config FREENETX_CPU_SELFTEST
        bool "Run a one-shot CPU tier self-test at boot"
        default n
        depends on FREENETX_CPU_SCALING
        help
            After boot, walk the CPU through the high, medium and idle tiers
            and log the frequency actually applied. Useful to verify that DFS
            works on a new board. It only runs once and then gets out of the
            way; leave it disabled in normal operation.

    config FREENETX_STATUS_LED_GPIO
        int "Status LED GPIO (-1 = disabled)"
        range -1 48
        default 2
        help
            GPIO driving the status LED. On the DOIT ESP32 DEVKIT V1 the
            on-board LED is on GPIO2 and is blue. The LED is solid on while
            the node is working, and blinks slowly while a configured uplink
            is disconnected. Use -1 if no LED is fitted.

    config FREENETX_STATUS_LED_ACTIVE_HIGH
        bool "Status LED is active high"
        default y
        help
            Enable if the LED lights when the GPIO is driven high. Disable for
            an active-low LED (e.g. some external LEDs wired to 3V3).

endmenu
